{"tool_name":"mptopoquerier","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"mptopoquerier","home":"http://blanco.biomol.uci.edu/mptopo/","summary":"Java applet developed for searching MPtopo, a curated database of membrane proteins with experimentally validated transmembrane (TM) segments. Retrieved sequences can be examined automatically by MPEx, a java-based hydropathy-plot tool.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:50:02Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:51Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:mptopoquerier","credit":[{"email":"stephen.white@uci.edu","name":"Stephen H. White","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://blanco.biomol.uci.edu/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://blanco.biomol.uci.edu/mptopo/"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deposition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3431"},{"term":"Query and retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0224"}]}],"name":"MPtopoQuerier","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"The reliability of the transmembrane (TM) sequence assignments for membrane proteins (MPs) in standard sequence databases is uncertain because the vast majority are based on hydropathy plots. A database of MPs with dependable assignments is necessary for developing new computational tools for the prediction of MP structure. We have therefore created MPtopo, a database of MPs whose topologies have been verified experimentally by means of crystallography, gene fusion, and other methods. Tests using MPtopo strongly validated four existing MP topology-prediction algorithms. MPtopo is freely available over the internet and can be queried by means of an SQL-based search engine.","authors":[{"name":"Hristova K."},{"name":"Jayasinghe S."},{"name":"White S.H."}],"citationCount":141,"date":"2001-03-31T00:00:00Z","journal":"Protein Science","tit